  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1100 PM CDT Fri Jun 19 2026\n\nA front trailing from the Ohio Valley low pressure system will\nbecome diffuse as it drops southward and stalls out over the TN \nValley Tuesday. A series of little waves will move along the \ndiffuse frontal zone with episodes of scattered showers and \nstorms through the week. A few diurnally strong storms could \noccur, but no organized severe storms are apparent after Monday. \nTemperatures and humidity levels will be pretty typical for this \ntime of year.",
